---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";

const stable = [
  ["version", "Package and milestone metadata."],
  ["doctor", "Check local environment and project layout."],
  ["review-map .", "Build the local review map (canonical first command)."],
  ["value-paths .", "Where value enters, moves, exits."],
  ["assumptions .", "Trust conditions each path depends on."],
  ["test-gap-map .", "Value-sensitive functions with missing tests, with Source: refs."],
  ["proof-plan .", "Local Foundry proof-scaffold directions."]
];
---

<Layout
  title="V4 release — ArkheionX"
  description="Arkheionx v4.0.0 stabilizes the local review-map workflow. What is stable, what stays experimental, and the known limitations."
>
  <main class="workflow-page">
    <section class="workflow-hero">
      <p class="workflow-kicker">V4 release</p>
      <h1>V4 stabilizes the local review-map workflow.</h1>
      <p>
        Arkheionx v4.0.0 is the milestone where the review-map path and its focused views are the
        stable, supported public surface. It does not mean ArkheionX guarantees protocol safety,
        confirms vulnerabilities, or replaces an audit. The package version is 4.0.0, tagged in
        git with a published GitHub release, and the site is live.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="workflow-command">
      <div>
        <p class="workflow-kicker">Stable in V4</p>
        <h2>The review workflow is supported.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow-command__stack">
        <pre><code>{stable.map((row) => `arkheionx ${row[0]}`).join("\n")}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="workflow-steps">
      <article>
        <span>EXP</span>
        <h2>Experimental / advanced</h2>
        <p>The source-tree commands <code>scan</code>, <code>test-plan</code>, and <code>search</code> are not the canonical first run and are not bundled in the installed wheel. Run them from a repository checkout.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>LIM</span>
        <h2>Known limitations</h2>
        <p>Static heuristics, not execution. Cross-contract value flow is surfaced as per-contract paths. Depth is shown on fixtures; real-protocol validation is planned.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>CHK</span>
        <h2>Validation</h2>
        <p>Docs links, safety wording, version consistency, release readiness, the full unit-test suite, <code>make validate</code>, and the site build all pass.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="workflow-command">
      <div>
        <p class="workflow-kicker">Try it</p>
        <h2>The bundled multi-contract demo.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow-command__stack">
        <pre><code>arkheionx review-map examples/vault-strategy-oracle-fixture</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="workflow-boundary">
      <p class="workflow-kicker">Next</p>
      <h2>After V4: engine sharpness and real-protocol proof.</h2>
      <p>
        The next focus is deeper cross-contract value flow and authorized real-protocol case
        studies. The full release package lives in the repository under
        <code>docs/releases/</code>, and the scope is in <code>docs/V4_STABLE_SCOPE.md</code>.
      </p>
      <a href="/roadmap" class="workflow-button">See the roadmap</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
